            }
          ],
          "question": {
            "text": "A parallel plate capacitor with plate area $A$ and plate separation $d$ is charged by constant current I. A plane surface of area $\\mathrm{A} / 2$, parallel to the plates is drawn simultaneously between the plates. The displacement current through this area is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "vmbNc",
              "text": "I",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "UrtMa",
              "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{I}}{2}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            },
            {
              "id": "3plmj",
              "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{I}}{4}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "S1Prf",
              "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{I}}{8}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "The electric field $E$ between the plates of a parallel plate capacitor is uniform and is given by $E = \\dfrac{q}{\\varepsilon_0 A}$, where $q$ is the charge on the capacitor plates and $A$ is the plate area.<br><br>The electric flux $\\Phi_E$ through a plane surface of area $A/2$ parallel to the plates is:<br><br>$\\Phi_E = E \\times \\dfrac{A}{2} = \\dfrac{q}{\\varepsilon_0 A} \\times \\dfrac{A}{2} = \\dfrac{q}{2\\varepsilon_0}$<br><br>The displacement current $I_d$ through this area is given by:<br><br>$I_d = \\varepsilon_0 \\dfrac{d\\Phi_E}{dt}$<br><br>Substituting the value of $\\Phi_E$:<br><br>$I_d = \\varepsilon_0 \\dfrac{d}{dt} \\left( \\dfrac{q}{2\\varepsilon_0} \\right) = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\dfrac{dq}{dt}$<br><br>Since the capacitor is being charged by a constant current $I$, the rate of change of charge is $\\dfrac{dq}{dt} = I$.<br><br>Therefore, the displacement current through the given area is:<br><br>$I_d = \\dfrac{I}{2}$<br><br>Answer: $\\frac{\\mathrm{I}}{2}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
