            }
          ],
          "question": {
            "text": "An electromagnetic wave, whose wave normal makes an angle of $45^{\\circ}$ with the vertical, travelling in air strikes a horizontal liquid surface. While travelling through the liquid it gets deviated through $15^{\\circ}$. What is the speed of the electromagnetic wave in the liquid, if the speed of electromagnetic wave in air is $3 \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$ ? $\\left(\\sin 30^{\\circ}=0 \\cdot 5, \\sin 45^{\\circ}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)$",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "RSIE3",
              "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "9J5C4",
              "text": "$1.5 \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "eo1gc",
              "text": "$2 \\cdot 1 \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            },
            {
              "id": "eQguC",
              "text": "$2.5 \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "The angle of incidence is $\\mathrm{i}=45^{\\circ}$\nThe angle of deviation is $\\delta=15^{\\circ}$\nThe angle of refraction is\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\delta=i-r \\\\\n& r=i-\\delta \\\\\n& r=45^{\\circ}-15^{\\circ} \\\\\n& r=30^{\\circ}\n\\end{aligned}$\nThe relation between the speed of the wave in the medium, the angle of incidence and the angle of refraction is given by the formula:\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{v}_2}{\\mathrm{v}_1}=\\frac{\\sin \\mathrm{r}}{\\sin \\mathrm{i}} \\\\\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{v}_2}{\\mathrm{v}_1}=\\frac{\\sin 30^{\\circ}}{\\sin 45^{\\circ}} \\\\\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{v}_2}{\\mathrm{v}_1}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{v}_2=\\frac{\\mathrm{v}_1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ & \\mathrm{v}_2=\\frac{3 \\times 10^8}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ & \\mathrm{v}_2=2.1 \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}\\end{aligned}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
          "questionStructure": [
            "default"
          ],
